    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes. `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented tenure-gated membership level 4 (previously reserved but never produced).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New `util/OwnerTenure.java`** \u2014 a small single-purpose unit that computes an owner's tenure in whole days from their `registrationDate` to today, returning `0` for a missing or not-yet-arrived date. This isolates the clock/date concern (matching the codebase's existing `LocalDate.now()` convention in `PetAgeValidator`/`ClinicServiceImpl`) away from the level arithmetic.\n\n2. **`util/MembershipLevelFormatter.java`** \u2014 the pre-tenure factors (email + no-namesakes) still cap at 3; it now adds a final level (reaching 4) when `OwnerTenure.inDays(registrationDate) > 365`. It delegates tenure computation to `OwnerTenure` rather than duplicating it. Constants renamed for clarity (`PRE_TENURE_MAX_LEVEL`, `TENURE_THRESHOLD_DAYS`).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 passes `owner.getRegistrationDate()` into the formatter.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipLevel` description and raised `maximum` from 3 to 4.\n\n**Why a new owner stays at level 3:** a freshly created owner's `registrationDate` is today (or the next business day), so tenure is `0` (future dates clamp to `0`), never exceeding 365 \u2014 so with an email and `namesakeCount == 0` they land at exactly level 3, regardless of household size. This is exactly what the `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test verifies, and it passes.",
